# Line-coverage floor, in percent. Read by .github/workflows/ci.yml and by tasks.ps1, so the gate
# a developer runs locally is the gate CI runs. One value, one file, no second copy to drift.
#
# Set from measurement, never invented. A threshold above the real number fails on day one and gets
# deleted; a threshold far below it lets coverage rot unnoticed, which is the same as having none.
# The rule here is: a few points under the measured value, so an honest refactor has room but a
# real regression trips it.
#
# Measured history — `./tasks.ps1 coverage` prints the current value:
#   2026-08-05   83.80%  (2261/2698)  715 tests
#   2026-08-05   86.53%  (2750/3178)  974 tests
#   2026-08-05   87.84%  (3562/4055)  1187 tests
#
# The weakest assembly is AppTemplate.Api at 78.51%; the total is what the gate enforces, so a large new
# controller with no tests can pull the total down even while every other project improves.
85
